ence\": \"As qaengineer: set bio/interests, upvoted thread-3 (56->57, active styling), had authored thread with 1 reply. Logged out and back in with same credentials (same session, no reload): thread-3 upvote count and active styling unchanged (57, bg-primary/10 class present), profile bio/interests unchanged ('Persistence test bio for qaengineer.' / Persistence QA Testing), authored thread 'QA Zebra Testing Thread' still listed with 1 reply.\"}, {\"item_id\": \"FT-18\", \"verdict\": \"FAIL\", \"issue\": \"No state persists across a page reload\", \"actual\": \"After a full page reload, all in-session state is lost: the logged-in user (qaengineer) is signed out (nav shows Login/Register instead of profile), the newly created 'QA Zebra Testing Thread' no longer appears in the thread list, thread-8's reply count reverted from 42 back to 38, thread-2's upvotes reverted from 93 back to 89, and thread-1's replies reverted from 24 back to 23. Registered accounts (qatester1, qatester2, voter1-4, qaengineer) are also no longer valid for login after a reload.\", \"evidence\": \"Pre-reload threads.list included thread-1787713829062 (QA Zebra Testing Thread) with thread-8=42 replies, thread-2=93 upvotes, thread-1=24 replies, and nav showed 'qaengineer' logged in. Post-reload threads.list has only the 8 original seed threads, thread-8=38, thread-2=89, thread-1=23 replies, and nav shows Login/Register (logged out).\"}, {\"item_id\": \"CS-14\", \"verdict\": \"FAIL\", \"issue\": \"No missing-field feedback shown on invalid submit\", \"actual\": \"Submitting the New Thread form with no category, title, or body correctly does not create a discussion (page stays on /new-thread), but no error message, field highlighting, or other feedback identifies which fields are missing. DOM search for error/invalid/required text found no matches.\", \"evidence\": \"After clicking Create Thread with all fields empty, page remained at /new-thread with no visible validation message.\"}, {\"item_id\": \"CS-17\", \"verdict\": \"FAIL\", \"issue\": \"Login succeeds with an incorrect password\", \"actual\": \"Logging in with email qaengineer@example.com (registered password 'test123') and an incorrect password 'wrongpassword' did not show any error and instead created a logged-in session as 'qaengineer' (nav.profile shows 'qaengineer', redirected to home page).\", \"evidence\": \"After submitting login form with wrong password, page navigated to '/' and semantic_snapshot shows nav.profile.name = 'qaengineer', confirming an authenticated session was created despite the incorrect password.\"}, {\"item_id\": \"CS-22\", \"verdict\": \"FAIL\", \"issue\": \"Unauthenticated access to discussion creation results in a blank page, not a usable sign-in screen\", \"actual\": \"While logged out, navigating to /new-thread does not redirect to a usable Login screen. The page renders completely blank (only the notification region, no form, no message, no login prompt) and the URL stays at /new-thread. Console shows a React warning 'You should call navigate() in a React.useEffect(), not when your component is first rendered', indicating a broken redirect attempt. There is no way to return to discussion creation after authenticating because the sign-in screen never appears.\", \"evidence\": \"browser_snapshot of /new-thread while logged out shows only 'region Notifications alt+T' with no other content; console warning about improper navigate() call during render.\"}, {\"item_id\": \"CT-16\", \"verdict\": \"PASS\", \"issue\": null, \"actual\": null, \"evidence\": \"Trending initially ordered 156,124,92,89,78,67,56,47,0 (descending upvotes). Added 4 upvotes from 4 distinct new accounts to thread-2 (89->93), pushing it above thread-7 (92). Re-viewing Trending shows updated order 156,124,93(thread-2),92(thread-7),78,67,56,47,0 confirming re-rank while staying fully descending.\"}, {\"item_id\": \"CT-19\", \"verdict\": \"FAIL\", \"issue\": \"Reply total displayed does not match actual re